# Dot Dash broker ACL
#
# With an acl_file present, mosquitto denies everything not listed here, so both
# accounts must be described in full.
#
# Both credentials are effectively public -- the device one is recoverable from
# the firmware images, the app one sits in a public HTML file -- so this limits
# what a leaked credential CAN DO rather than keeping it secret.
#
# What a shared device credential cannot express is "only my own topics". That
# needs one username per device (username = hashedMyID, plus pattern ACLs).
# Until then, devices can still read each other's msg/ and cmd/ topics.

# ---------------- Parent application ----------------
# The moderator: sends commands, claims devices, relays messages, reads Monitor.
user dotdash-app
topic write     doorbell/cmd/+
topic write     doorbell/pairing/+
topic read      doorbell/pairing/reply/+
topic readwrite doorbell/msg/+
topic readwrite doorbell/msg/+/#
topic readwrite doorbell/monitor/+/#
topic read      doorbell/presence/+

# ---------------- Devices ----------------
user DigitalDoorbell
topic readwrite doorbell/msg/+
topic readwrite doorbell/msg/+/#
topic readwrite doorbell/presence/+
topic readwrite doorbell/score/+/+

# Monitor is WRITE ONLY. Devices never subscribe to it, and it carries message
# text plus the recipient hash -- so a leaked device credential must not be able
# to read that stream back.
topic write     doorbell/monitor/+/#

# cmd stays readwrite: a device clears its own retained command by publishing an
# empty payload to it, which is what stops a retained GRANT_TIMER being
# re-awarded on every reconnect. Cannot be narrowed without per-device usernames.
topic readwrite doorbell/cmd/+

# Pairing: devices READ their own pairing topic and WRITE only to reply/.
# Deliberately no write on doorbell/pairing/+ -- that is the CLAIM topic, and a
# leaked credential must not be able to claim an unpaired device out from under
# its parent. The two sit at different depths, so the ACL can tell them apart.
topic read      doorbell/pairing/+
topic write     doorbell/pairing/reply/+

# ---------------- Push bridge ----------------
# Forwards friendreq / timerreq / battery alerts to parents' phones via FCM,
# because iOS suspends the parent app and its MQTT connection with it.
#
# READ ONLY, and only Monitor. It never publishes anything, so it never should
# be able to: a leaked bridge credential can watch that stream and nothing else.
# Note this is the one stream carrying message text, which is why it gets its
# own account rather than reusing the device or app credentials.
user dotdash-bridge
topic read      doorbell/monitor/+/#
